Yamahi, you taught her some weird fishing,
so now the poor girl is confused.

00:13:27.430 --> 00:13:29.430
I-It's not weird!

00:13:29.430 --> 00:13:33.350
I know! When it's Obon,
want to go to my grandma's place?

00:13:33.350 --> 00:13:35.560
There's a mountain stream nearby.

00:13:35.560 --> 00:13:39.940
Wow, yes! I still need to fish!

00:13:39.940 --> 00:13:43.110
Our summer vacation's just begun.

00:13:52.370 --> 00:13:56.870
Okay, let's get Futaba and
Ichika's fly fishing debut underway!

00:13:56.870 --> 00:13:58.830
Thanks for having us here today.

00:13:58.830 --> 00:14:01.750
N-Now, then. Let's practice casting.

00:14:01.750 --> 00:14:02.670
Okay.

00:14:02.670 --> 00:14:05.590
Let's go over there
so we won't get in anyone's way.

00:14:05.590 --> 00:14:06.420
Okay.

00:14:06.420 --> 00:14:10.390
This seems like a normal river, but
it's a designated fishing place, right?

00:14:10.390 --> 00:14:11.850
The water's so pretty!

00:14:11.850 --> 00:14:14.220
This place takes advantage
of the clear stream.

00:14:14.220 --> 00:14:17.640
This is basically as close to
nature as you can get fishing.

00:14:17.640 --> 00:14:19.230
Huh...

00:14:19.230 --> 00:14:20.860
Huh? What's that?

00:14:20.860 --> 00:14:23.230
Someone who works here.

00:14:23.230 --> 00:14:26.780
Whoa! That truck has a lot of fish in it!

00:14:26.780 --> 00:14:28.780
Stop pointing.

00:14:28.780 --> 00:14:31.780
They release more fish into
the water every now and then.

00:14:32.990 --> 00:14:34.950
Because they've just been
released into the water,

00:14:34.950 --> 00:14:40.000
most of those fish won't know what
to expect. Perfect time to catch them.

00:14:40.000 --> 00:14:41.750
They won't?

00:14:41.750 --> 00:14:46.090
Basically, they're fish that haven't
been caught yet, so their guard is down.

00:14:46.090 --> 00:14:50.930
Okay, I'm gonna catch those pure and
innocent fish with some artificial bait!

00:14:50.930 --> 00:14:52.640
Do you have to say it like that?

00:14:54.350 --> 00:14:55.890
Hup!

00:14:57.270 --> 00:14:59.980
Your casting's gotten better.

00:14:59.980 --> 00:15:03.110
I've been practicing a lot!

00:15:03.110 --> 00:15:05.530
Huh? My fly is going downstream.

00:15:05.530 --> 00:15:10.240
Yup. This is what's different
than a designated area at a lake.

00:15:10.240 --> 00:15:12.870
Of course, it's going to go
downstream because it's a river,

00:15:12.870 --> 00:15:16.160
but fly lines are meant
to flow down even easier,

00:15:16.160 --> 00:15:19.370
which makes the line
move in front of the fly.

00:15:19.370 --> 00:15:20.500
When that happens,

00:15:20.500 --> 00:15:24.630
the fly moves in an unnatural way
because it's getting pulled by the line.

00:15:24.670 --> 00:15:26.090
"You won't fool me"

00:15:26.090 --> 00:15:27.010
"You won't fool me"
As you can figure, the fish
will be guarded and won't bite.

00:15:27.010 --> 00:15:29.590
As you can figure, the fish
will be guarded and won't bite.

00:15:29.590 --> 00:15:31.720
Then what am I supposed to do?

00:15:31.720 --> 00:15:35.560
That's when you use
a technique called mending.

00:15:35.560 --> 00:15:36.510
Huh?

00:15:36.510 --> 00:15:37.970
Go ahead and cast your line,

00:15:37.970 --> 00:15:39.770
and once your fly lands in the water,

00:15:39.770 --> 00:15:42.770
pull up your line and tilt it upstream.

00:15:42.770 --> 00:15:46.860
Then, as you can see,
the line will flow after the fly.

00:15:46.860 --> 00:15:50.530
It'll flow naturally
without it getting pulled.

00:15:50.530 --> 00:15:52.070
I'll give it a shot!

00:15:53.070 --> 00:15:56.330
I cast, and once my fly
lands in the water,

00:15:56.330 --> 00:16:00.160
I pull up my line and whoa! Why though?!

00:16:00.160 --> 00:16:04.250
Once your line hits the
water's surface, it's hard to lift up,

00:16:04.250 --> 00:16:07.630
so you'll want to lift it up
as soon as the fly lands.

00:16:07.630 --> 00:16:10.550
You'll get a better idea on how much
strength you need the more you do it.

00:16:10.550 --> 00:16:12.760
Yeah! Just like that!

00:16:12.760 --> 00:16:14.550
You sure are a quick learner.

00:16:14.550 --> 00:16:16.510
Thank you very much.

00:16:18.140 --> 00:16:21.140
It's getting hotter,
so it's getting harder to fish.

00:16:21.140 --> 00:16:23.350
Why don't we take a break for a while?

00:16:24.400 --> 00:16:29.150
Ichika, you've been wearing
that pendant for a while.

00:16:29.150 --> 00:16:32.110
Well, it's a gift from my precious Futaba!

00:16:32.110 --> 00:16:35.200
My sister's been wearing it ever since.

00:16:35.200 --> 00:16:37.830
It looks very nice on you.

00:16:37.830 --> 00:16:42.710
Aiko said that her mom was really
happy when she gave her the ring, too!

00:16:42.710 --> 00:16:45.420
A ring, huh?

00:16:45.420 --> 00:16:48.460
Our parents don't wear
wedding bands, do they?

00:16:48.460 --> 00:16:50.010
Now that you mention it...

00:16:50.010 --> 00:16:53.880
Like they bought them and just don't
wear them? That's how my parents are.

00:16:53.880 --> 00:16:55.180
Oh, really?

00:16:55.180 --> 00:16:59.350
Apparently when my dad first tried
fishing with his on, it was super awkward,

00:16:59.350 --> 00:17:00.720
so he's taken it off since.

00:17:00.720 --> 00:17:03.270
My mom took hers off to go along with him,

00:17:03.270 --> 00:17:05.980
but they always wear them
on necklaces instead.

00:17:05.980 --> 00:17:07.150
I see.

00:17:07.150 --> 00:17:11.110
My mom used to wear her old one, though.

00:17:11.110 --> 00:17:15.070
Then maybe they didn't buy them.

00:17:15.070 --> 00:17:17.870
I wonder if they're worried
about how we'd feel.

00:17:17.870 --> 00:17:22.000
Did you two congratulate
them on their marriage?

00:17:22.000 --> 00:17:23.000
Huh?

00:17:23.000 --> 00:17:25.790
I know we said how nice it'd be
to spend time together but...

00:17:25.790 --> 00:17:28.130
Then you should get on that.

00:17:28.130 --> 00:17:32.760
Yeah. Sometimes, things don't get
through to others unless they're said.

00:17:35.720 --> 00:17:39.390
I see... So they didn't
actually have a wedding.

00:17:39.390 --> 00:17:42.640
Yeah. We did have a dinner though.

00:17:42.640 --> 00:17:44.520
And I guess this is a second
marriage for both of them.

00:17:44.520 --> 00:17:48.480
Aw, but I'd love to see
your mom in a wedding dress.

00:17:48.480 --> 00:17:51.070
My mom in a dress, huh...

00:17:51.070 --> 00:17:54.030
And then enjoy a fancy full-course meal.

00:17:55.820 --> 00:17:59.320
Hiyori! Let's hold
a wedding for them tonight!

00:17:59.320 --> 00:18:00.370
What now?

00:18:00.370 --> 00:18:04.660
We're going to make a wedding
dinner with the fish we catch!

00:18:04.660 --> 00:18:06.790
And then we can congratulate them!

00:18:06.790 --> 00:18:08.290
Sure...

00:18:08.290 --> 00:18:11.090
But I'm going to be
with Futaba and Ichika,

00:18:11.090 --> 00:18:14.300
so do you think you'll be able
to catch enough for four?

00:18:14.300 --> 00:18:16.470
I-I'll do my best!

00:18:19.090 --> 00:18:22.140
They seem to be having
better luck over there.

00:18:23.810 --> 00:18:25.480
No!

00:18:25.480 --> 00:18:27.940
Crap! I wasn't paying attention!

00:18:27.940 --> 00:18:32.360
Calm down, Koharu! Just remember
everything you've been taught until now.

00:18:32.360 --> 00:18:35.440
Don't put any strength into it,

00:18:35.440 --> 00:18:37.650
and don't flail around too much.

00:18:40.370 --> 00:18:42.950
There! That was really nice!

00:18:44.740 --> 00:18:47.710
Come on... come on!

00:18:49.170 --> 00:18:52.170
Th-There!

00:18:52.170 --> 00:18:56.720
Calm down! Pull in the line
so it doesn't sag too much!

00:18:58.510 --> 00:19:01.640
I got one!

00:19:01.640 --> 00:19:04.470
Yay! Just three more!

00:19:04.470 --> 00:19:06.890
I can do this!

00:19:07.890 --> 00:19:11.440
Koharu-<i>chan </i>asked us to put on some white
dress clothes and wait a while, but...

00:19:11.440 --> 00:19:13.820
I wonder what she's up to.

00:19:13.820 --> 00:19:18.030
Sorry. She can be rather
spontaneous at times.

00:19:20.200 --> 00:19:23.870
You can come down now, you two.

00:19:23.870 --> 00:19:26.240
Koharu, what are you--

00:19:27.250 --> 00:19:29.290
Happy four months and
three days into your marriage!

00:19:29.290 --> 00:19:31.710
Congratulations!

00:19:31.710 --> 00:19:32.670
Oh, my.

00:19:32.670 --> 00:19:35.050
What a rather... random date.

00:19:35.050 --> 00:19:37.460
Well, they say no time like the present!

00:19:37.460 --> 00:19:38.420
Also...

00:19:38.420 --> 00:19:41.340
Ichika paid for the flowers!

00:19:41.340 --> 00:19:42.390
What?

00:19:42.390 --> 00:19:44.760
Come on, Daddy. Have a seat!

00:19:44.760 --> 00:19:46.850
I'll hold onto the flowers for you.

00:19:46.850 --> 00:19:49.180
Wait, what is all of this?

00:19:50.640 --> 00:19:52.770
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:19:52.770 --> 00:19:54.980
Here's your appetizer, caprese.

00:19:54.980 --> 00:19:56.570
Wow, it looks authentic.

00:19:56.570 --> 00:20:00.700
It really does. Hiyori, your clothes...

00:20:00.700 --> 00:20:02.700
Please don't say anything! Jeez!

00:20:02.700 --> 00:20:06.330
Koharu's the one who suggested this!

00:20:06.330 --> 00:20:10.000
First, I sprinkle some salt and <i>arabiki</i>
black pepper onto some rainbow trout,

00:20:10.000 --> 00:20:16.000
then I season the inside,
and lightly flour both sides.

00:20:16.000 --> 00:20:19.760
Put the frying pan on medium heat,
throw on some vegetable oil,

00:20:19.760 --> 00:20:24.680
put in the rainbow trout, then shake the
pan as I grill them so they don't burn.

00:20:24.680 --> 00:20:27.640
Once both sides are brown,
pour in some butter,

00:20:27.640 --> 00:20:30.020
and let the oil go all around the pan.

00:20:31.270 --> 00:20:33.190
That smells lovely.

00:20:34.810 --> 00:20:40.240
Thank you for waiting. Here is your
main dish: rainbow trout meunière.

00:20:40.240 --> 00:20:42.490
My!

00:20:42.490 --> 00:20:43.990
Wow.

00:20:45.620 --> 00:20:47.280
It's delicious!

00:20:48.330 --> 00:20:49.540
I'd like to speak to the chef.

00:20:49.540 --> 00:20:51.410
Right here! That's me!

00:20:52.540 --> 00:20:53.920
Thank you.

00:20:55.670 --> 00:20:58.630
It's very delicious.

00:21:00.300 --> 00:21:02.420
You're very welcome!

00:21:03.380 --> 00:21:06.930
Wow... their display of
affection sure is something.

00:21:06.930 --> 00:21:10.020
Hiyori, was Koharu
able to catch any today?

00:21:10.020 --> 00:21:16.060
I was with Futaba and Ichika the
whole time, so Koharu caught all of this.

00:21:16.060 --> 00:21:17.940
Ah, I see.

00:21:17.940 --> 00:21:20.570
You're a great waitress, Hiyori.

00:21:20.570 --> 00:21:23.900
Can we drop that already?

00:21:23.900 --> 00:21:24.990
We did it!

00:21:24.990 --> 00:21:26.320
Yeah.

00:21:27.450 --> 00:21:29.830
We even baked you a wedding cake.

00:21:29.830 --> 00:21:31.910
What?

00:21:31.910 --> 00:21:34.710
Happy wedding!

00:21:40.800 --> 00:21:43.260
Good morning...

00:21:43.260 --> 00:21:44.420
Late morning!

00:21:44.420 --> 00:21:45.970
It's already noon!

00:21:45.970 --> 00:21:48.930
It's summer vacation, so that's fine.

00:21:48.930 --> 00:21:49.140
"Hand-stretched <i>somen</i>"

00:21:49.140 --> 00:21:51.560
"Hand-stretched <i>somen</i>"
Why don't we have some
cold <i>somen </i>noodles for lunch?

00:21:51.560 --> 00:21:52.430
"Hand-stretched <i>somen</i>"
Sure.

00:21:52.430 --> 00:21:53.770
Want to make some sesame dipping sauce?

00:21:53.770 --> 00:21:55.100
Sure.

00:21:55.100 --> 00:21:58.150
They seem so chipper.

00:21:58.150 --> 00:22:01.400
Are you two really not
going to have a wedding?

00:22:01.400 --> 00:22:04.240
Oh, we don't need to!

00:22:04.240 --> 00:22:07.990
How are we going to
top yesterday's ceremony?

00:22:11.580 --> 00:22:15.250
Since we're all off today,
why don't we take a trip somewhere?

00:22:15.250 --> 00:22:16.870
Then let's go fishing!

00:22:16.870 --> 00:22:18.210
I think that's a great idea!

00:22:18.210 --> 00:22:19.880
I wonder if I can catch anything.

00:22:19.880 --> 00:22:23.710
Don't worry! We'll show you the ropes!

00:22:30.180 --> 00:22:32.760
<i>Even if you don't say anything</i>

00:22:32.760 --> 00:22:38.520
<i>I know how you're feeling and</i>
<i>when you're lying or telling the truth</i>

00:22:38.520 --> 00:22:41.150
<i>Even if you don't do anything</i>

00:22:41.150 --> 00:22:46.150
<i>Just being next to you</i>
<i>makes the day brighter</i>

00:22:46.150 --> 00:22:50.370
<i>The reason I've always loved the ocean</i>

00:22:50.370 --> 00:22:55.120
<i>Is because you were always by my side</i>

00:22:55.120 --> 00:22:58.330
<i>The way we laugh is becoming similar</i>

00:22:58.330 --> 00:23:03.460
<i>It's almost like we're cider</i>

00:23:03.460 --> 00:23:07.670
<i>Bubble, bubble, our laughter combines</i>

00:23:07.670 --> 00:23:11.970
<i>Bubble, bubble, then floats up</i>
<i>and pops together</i>

00:23:11.970 --> 00:23:20.230
<i>We gather up the light and</i>
<i>gain even more precious things</i>

00:23:20.230 --> 00:23:24.480
<i>Bubble, bubble, our laughter combines</i>

00:23:24.480 --> 00:23:28.820
<i>Bubble, bubble, then floats up</i>
<i>and pops together</i>

00:23:28.820 --> 00:23:33.780
<i>May a present where we can</i>
<i>laugh about the past and future</i>

00:23:33.780 --> 00:23:39.910
<i>Always be right here</i>

00:23:41.460 --> 00:23:46.460
<i>May a present where we can</i>
<i>laugh about the past and future</i>

00:23:46.460 --> 00:23:52.840
<i>Always be right here</i>

00:23:54.970 --> 00:23:56.060
"Next Time"

00:23:56.060 --> 00:23:59.730
"Next Time"
Hey, Futaba! We used
some krill to fish today,

00:23:59.730 --> 00:24:01.600
"Next Time"
but what other kind of bait is there?

00:24:01.600 --> 00:24:04.360
"Next Time"
Hm... Maybe some eunicids?

00:24:04.360 --> 00:24:06.440
"Next Time"
Eunicids? I'll search for that right now!

00:24:06.440 --> 00:24:09.530
"Next Time"
Wait, no!

00:24:09.530 --> 00:24:09.940
"Next Time"
